The mux conflict panic has been resolved — all tests pass except `TestCreateLink`. It fails because `short_url` = `://127.0.0.1:25502/P6Oo2g` — the scheme is missing. `r.URL.Scheme` is always empty for server-side requests (the scheme is not included in the request line). It needs to be obtained from `r.TLS != nil` or from the `X-Forwarded-Proto` header. The test expects `http://...`.

Let's check handlers.go to fix this. Standard approach:

```go
scheme := "http"
if r.TLS != nil {
    scheme = "https"
} else if p := r.Header.Get("X-Forwarded-Proto"); p != "" {
    scheme = p
}
```

In the test, requests are sent over plain http to 127.0.0.1, so scheme = "http". Good.

